BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Day 10
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260214T150000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260214T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001219-1771081200-1771110000@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/01/Screenshot-2026-01-20-at-12.51.19-pm.png
CREATED:20260120T015238Z
DESCRIPTION:Day 10\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 – RONA. / Alfred Czital & 
 Ayū / Helhur / Trae Bashford / Eldest \n\n\n\nAnd just like that\, we’r
 e at number 10! \n\n\n\nThis will be a special one\, if you were lucky eno
 ugh to catch RONA’s set at Meredith\, you’ll know why \n\n\n\nJoining 
 the bill all the way from Berlin with a live set is Alfred Czital and Ayū
  along with some of our favourite locals \n\n\n\nRONA. \n\n\n\nRONA. is a 
 Kaytetye producer and DJ whose sound is deeply grounded in the vast desert
  landscapes of her home\, Mparntwein central ‘Australia’. \n\n\n\nBlen
 ding the rhythms and landscapes of desert Country with the pulse of club c
 ulture\, she crafts immersive sonic experiences that are driven from her l
 ife moving between many worlds. Since her breakout 2022 release\, Closure\
 , RONA. has emerged as a force in electronic music\, building a catalogue 
 that channels the deep storylines she’s connected to. Her Ancestors soun
 dtracked the first sunrise and she continues their legacy\, exploring rhyt
 hm\, sovereignty in sound\, and oral storytelling in evolving ways. A soni
 c and visual storyteller\, RONA. layers synths with the textures of Countr
 y\, creating journeys that resonate with the soul and move dance floors. \
 n\n\n\nHer latest releases\, Raise It and Burn It\, push sonic boundaries 
 in her practice while amplifying movements for First Nations justice and l
 iberation. With a growing presence alongside beloved electronic artists li
 ke Four Tet and Overmono\, RONA. has left her mark on major festivals\, in
 cluding Laneway\, Pitch Music & Arts\, Strawberry Fields\, and Splendour i
 n the Grass. RONA. is an artist creating music that centres connections to
  Country\, self\, and place across generations. \n\n\n\nAlfred Czital & Ay
 ū \n\n\n\nBerlin-based producers Alfred Czital and Ayū joined forces in 
 2023 to create a distinctive live project under the umbrella of Harmony Re
 c. Known for their wide-ranging explorations of trance\, their performance
 s blend deep atmospheres with driving grooves\, crafting an experience tha
 t balances intensity with subtle detail. Each set is designed as a journey
 - immersive\, evolving\, and firmly rooted in the dancefloor. \n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for all. Ga
 ng Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We have z
 ero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to ensure 
 everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\, plea
 se contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for everyone
 . \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people\, t
 he Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We pay 
 our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and recognise
  their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are gra
 teful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260120T015650Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/3133/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TOPS
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260221T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260221T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001198-1771700400-1771714800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 25/12/Screenshot-2025-12-02-at-9.41.41-am.png
CREATED:20251201T224319Z
DESCRIPTION:When we first started Gang Gang\, it was during COVID\, we wer
 e working everyday and TOPS were spinning a lot. To think we’ve gone fro
 m those early 25 pax covid shows to booking TOPS to play at Gang Gang is w
 ild. \n\n\n\nCome get amongst it with us \n\n\n\nTOPS \n\n\n\nTOPS (CA) mu
 sicians David Carriere\, Jane Penny\, Marta Cikojevic\, and Riley Fleck\,
  write timeless music that reliably threads immediacy and depth. Bury the
  Key\, their first full-length since 2020 and with new label home Ghostly 
 International\, is a captivating reintroduction for the Montréal band: e
 ver refined\, undoubtedly masters of their melodic craft yet unafraid of 
 evolving and testing themselves against different\, at times darker tones.
  The album faces feelings once locked away\, engaging the give-and-take be
 tween happiness\, hedonism\, and self-destruction.While often inhabited by
  fictional figures\, their glowing\, grooving\, self-produced songs draw f
 rom personal observations: intimacy (both inside and outside the band)\, t
 oxic behavior\, drug use\, and apocalyptic dread. When recording started\,
  they noticed a shift and leaned in\, jokingly dubbed “evil TOPS\,” sa
 ys Penny. “We’re always kind of seen as a soft band or like naive or f
 riendly in a Canadian way\, but we made it a challenge to really channel t
 he world around us.” Through the lens of a looming epoch and the clarity
  that comes with age\, TOPS dip into a more sinister disco realm with Bury
  the Key\, giving their soft-focus sophisti-pop a sharpened edge. \n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for all
 . Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We ha
 ve zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to ens
 ure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\, 
 please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for ever
 yone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people
 \, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We 
 pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and recog
 nise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are
  grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251201T224321Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/tops/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Day 11
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260228T160000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260228T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001228-1772294400-1772319600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/02/Screenshot-2026-02-02-at-12.09.04-pm.png
CREATED:20260202T011150Z
DESCRIPTION:We’d usually give the cf (cafe floor) a few months to recove
 r from a day party. But we got the opportunity to bring you DJ Masda on Fe
 b 28\, sooo why let the dust settle. Day Eleven. DJ Masda\, Tim Heaney\, a
 nd GGG. \n\n\n\nDJ Masda ( @hauznated ) is one of the finest selectors in
  the Japanese underground scene\, if not the world. Flawless track selecti
 on\, precise mixing and the best of the old and the new\, DJ Masda is a de
 ep explorer. \n\n\n\nJoining DJ Masda is local og and owner of @vessel_for
 themessage Tim Heaney\, and a spearhead of Canberra’s party scene GGG ( 
 @groovegratitudeangouda ) \n\n\n\nCome early\, stay late. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 Gang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for all. Gang G
 ang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We have zero 
 tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to ensure ever
 yone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\, please c
 ontact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for everyone. \n
 \n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people\, the T
 raditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We pay our 
 respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and recognise the
 ir enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are gratefu
 l to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T011151Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/day-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annahstasia
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260301T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260301T220000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001206-1772388000-1772402400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 25/12/Screenshot-2025-12-21-at-11.19.47-am.png
CREATED:20251221T002202Z
DESCRIPTION:Annahstasia arrives in Australia for the first time this Febru
 ary\, bringing her soulful\, poetic\, and deeply intimate songcraft to sta
 ges across the country. A singular voice in contemporary folk\, she has ca
 rved her own path through patience\, independence\, and a devotion to stor
 ytelling – qualities that shape her acclaimed debut album Tether. \n\n\
 n\nTether is a record built slowly and intentionally\, recorded live at V
 alentine Studios in Los Angeles with a community of collaborators includin
 g Jason Lader\, Andrew Lappin\, Aaron Liao\, Obongjayar\, and aja mon
 et. Across its sweeping arrangements and bare\, vulnerable moments\, Annah
 stasia’s voice sits at the centre: rich\, resonant\, and unguarded. Her 
 songs navigate love in all its forms – the love we find\, lose\, resist\
 , and rebuild – approached with the nuance of poetry and a quiet\, assur
 ed power. \n\n\n\nIn February\, Australian audiences will have the chance 
 to experience this world up close. Annahstasia will perform headline shows
  in Melbourne\, Sydney\, Perth and Canberra\, alongside special appearanc
 es at Meeniyan Town Hall\, Port Fairy Folk Festival\, and WOMADelaide. It
  marks her long-awaited introduction to Australian stages\, and a rare opp
 ortunity to witness an artist whose work feels both intimate and expansive
 . \n\n\n\nOnstage\, Annahstasia performs with the same instinct and openne
 ss that shaped Tether. Her sets move between stillness and swelling emoti
 on\, carried by a voice that can shift from gentle warmth to something bre
 athtakingly commanding. Each performance becomes its own moment – lived\
 , shared\, and fleeting. \n\n\n\nAnnahstasia’s debut Australian tour is 
 a celebration of an artist stepping into her full creative force. \n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for all
 . Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We ha
 ve zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to ens
 ure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\, 
 please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for ever
 yone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people
 \, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We 
 pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and recog
 nise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are
  grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251221T002204Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/annahstasia/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:James K with Alias Error & friends
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260306T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260306T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001207-1772823600-1772838000@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 25/12/Screenshot-2025-12-21-at-11.23.05-am.png
CREATED:20251221T002441Z
DESCRIPTION:This is a really special one for us. James K\, E Fishpool\, Mi
 cah Heathwood x Umki. Having them come together at Gang Gang feels like a 
 rare alignment. These are  artists who move with their own gravity and in
 tention. Come\, lean in\, and listen. \n\n\n\nJames K \n\n\n\nA version of
  james K was born. Comprised of bones\, reactive metals and a larynx with 
 freckled eyes that catalyzes that mix\, she can now see through all the sc
 hemes. This is the truth. When she chews gum\, it’s not clear which one 
 of her personas does it. Since their first release in 2013\, describing th
 em separately is grunt work as they switch places\, cosplay each other and
  would most likely lull you into a lonesome dream. Together\, they know ho
 w to produce\, sound\, film and edit. Thus\, they are brought to the table
 \, performing and DJing in clubs and theaters\, along composers and childr
 en alike. She has performed in festivals and venues such as Dekmantel\, Su
 stain Release\, Mutek\, iii Points\, and Nowadays.. In recent years she ha
 s shared the stage with james Ferraro\, Robert Aiki Aubrey Lowe\, Yves Tum
 or\, Morton Subotnick\, Nick Leon\, and Priori\, among many others. \n\n\n
 \nShe has released with labels such as AD 93\, Incienso\, PAN\, iDEAL\, Di
 al\, UNO\, among others\, and started her label She Rocks! in 2015. Her co
 llaboration with hoodie\, a 10” titled ‘Scorpio\,’ was released in s
 ummer 2023 via AD 93\, landing on numerous EOTY lists. She followed up wit
 h another single\, trip-hop gem\, ‘Blinkmoth (July Mix)\,’ which has g
 arnered similar attention\, landing at number 2 on Resident Advisor’s 
 ‘Best Tracks of 2024\,’ and numerous other EOY lists\, the former publ
 ication naming her producer of the year. K has been a resident on NTS\, wi
 th her show\, ‘Trip Lick\,’ since 2019\, and she has provided mix’s 
 for series such as Dekmantel\, Crack and Fact. She is sought after for her
  signature magnetic vocals\, lyricism and production and\, through collabo
 rations\, has created critically acclaimed music with artists such as Moin
 \, Fergus Jones + Huerco S.\, Priori\, Special Guest DJ\, Yves Tumor\, Dre
 w McDowall\, LEYA\, and many others. She produces music that makes tempora
 ry haven for indomitable lyrics – and these are in constant flux. You ca
 n check what they are here: [917 908-1173]. It’s only a part of her fair
 ly detailed world. A world that she abandons and then builds upon. \n\n\n\
 n𝒮𝑜𝓂𝑒𝓉𝒾𝓂𝑒𝓈 𝓎𝑜𝓊 𝒸𝒶𝓃’𝓉 
 𝒽𝑒𝒶𝓇 𝓉𝒽𝑒 𝓌𝑜𝓇𝒹𝓈……𝓈𝒾𝓃𝒸
 𝑒 𝒶𝓃𝓎𝓉𝒽𝒾𝓃𝑔 𝒷𝑒𝓎𝑜𝓃𝒹 𝑒𝓋
 𝑒𝓇𝓎𝓉𝒽𝒾𝓃𝑔 𝓈𝒽𝑒 𝓌𝒶𝓃𝓉𝓈 𝓉
 𝑜 𝑔𝒾𝓋𝑒 𝓎𝑜𝓊 𝒶 𝒽𝒾𝓃𝓉……𝒾𝓉
 ’𝓈 𝓃𝑜𝓉 𝓅𝓇𝑒𝓉𝓉𝓎 (𝒷𝓊𝓉 𝒾𝓉
 ’𝓈 𝓅𝓇𝑒𝓉𝓉𝓎). \n\n\n\nTake a sip of water before you
 r memory error blinks. Dial to K. Listen to the disfragmented territory an
 d the cast of it she’s making. It might not be what you will have though
 t tomorrow. \n\n\n\nAlias Error  \n\n\n\nAlias Error\, is a singer\, song
 writer and DJ currently based in Berlin. As the lead singer and principal 
 songwriter of the duo a.s.o.\, Alia released an eponymous debut album in 2
 023 to critical acclaim.  \n\n\n\nIn 2024\, Alias Error kicked off the ye
 ar collaborating with alt-indie stalwart RIP Swirl\, lending her signature
  hypnotic vocals to the single “I Found You Out” from his sophomore al
 bum Perfectly Blue. Anchored by Alia’s unique voice\, her words speak of
  restraint and release\, moving fluidly from the elegiac to the euphoric a
 nd further cementing Alias Error’s position as an uncompromising rising 
 star in the electronic and alt-pop scene. Most recently\, she featured on 
 JASSS’s Eager Buyers EP\, released to high acclaim in September. The tra
 ck “It’s A Hole” gestures toward the dark\, atmospheric and cerebral
  world she will fully inhabit in the coming year. \n\n\n\nAlias Error is n
 ow gearing up for her first solo record that will be released in 2026\, Th
 e record looks to mould all of Alia’s influences into a singular express
 ion – at once powerful and nimble\, and unlike anything else. Spanning e
 ffortlessly between ethereal dream-pop to the more moodier corners of elec
 tronic spaces\, Alias Error will be collaborating with acclaimed producers
  Sepehr\, Priori\, Ben Bondy\, to name a few.  \n\n\n\nE-Fishpool \n\n\n\
 nE Fishpool is a boundary-pushing live performer\, by  many accounts Eora
 ’s best kept secret. They craft a unique live/hybrid set\, introducing 
 something different each time they perform. E Fishpool was one of the firs
 t electronic acts we had a Gang Gang (many years ago now)\, so we are stok
 ed to host them again.  \n\n\n\nMicah Heathwood x Umki \n\n\n\nMicah Heat
 hwood and Umki are two of Canberra’s most loved and unique artists. Mica
 h Heathwood\, through his solo project\, notably toured earlier this year 
 with Kamasi Washington\, while Umki has recently returned from their own i
 nternational tour in 2025. Both artists are forward-thinking and firmly es
 tablished within their respective worlds. \n\n\n\nMicah and Umki have perf
 ormed a small selection of special live shows in the past\, most recently 
 in 2023 alongside YL Hooi. Their collaborations are rare\, making them a m
 ust see.  \n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experi
 ence for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible rest
 rooms. We have zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in 
 place to ensure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or a
 ssistance\, please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoy
 able for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal peopl
 e\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. W
 e pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and rec
 ognise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We a
 re grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country. \n\n\n\nWe 
 offer equity tickets (low cost) to those who need\, and free tickets to al
 l First Nations\, we request please send an email to gigs@ganggangcafe.co
 m.au to purchase/ receive either ticket.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251221T002442Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/james-k-with-alias-error-friends/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ruby Gill + Mimi Gilbert (Poetry)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260315T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260315T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001226-1773597600-1773615600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/02/Screenshot-2026-02-02-at-12.01.20-pm.png
CREATED:20260202T010428Z
DESCRIPTION:Don’t miss Mimi Gilbert (USA) and Ruby Gill (Australia /
  South Africa) and as they embark on a once-in-a-lifetime\, intimate tour 
 of Australia this autumn\, bringing their award-winning alt-folk and profo
 und poetry to an exciting series of shows in big and small places near you
 . The two opinionated\, light-hearted\, torch-carriers of language have b
 een fast friends for many years\, and will be reuniting for an intimate to
 ur across Australia this March and April. For Mimi Gilbert\, this is a lau
 nch tour for their new record ‘Undrowning\,’ a record made between C
 alifornia and Australia. In support\, Ruby will be performing a new\, neve
 r-before-seen set of mostly spoken-word poetry (and a few songs)\, celebra
 ting the release of their new poetry book ‘I’m not exaggerating when 
 I say’.  \n\n\n\nThis experience is bound to be unforgettable – each 
 artist will bring their own flawless minimalism and unforgettable lyrical 
 honesty to the table\, with protest songs\, witnessing of nature\, explora
 tion of queerness and deep love for family and politics that are beloved b
 y audiences all over the globe. Both will leave you a little changed from 
 when you walked in the door. \n\n\n\nMore about Mimi Gilbert  \n\n\n\nMim
 i Gilbert is an independent artist who has spent the better part of the la
 st 10 years living\, touring and creating music in the USA\, Australia and
  New Zealand. Previously based in Melbourne now back in Ojai/ Los Angeles\
 , the Californian born has toured most recently with Julia Jacklin and Ang
 ie McMahon. Mimi shares a deeply-crafted\, folk-inflected approach to thei
 r songwriting. \n\n\n\nPronounced ‘the best kept secret in the music ind
 ustry’ by Double J – Australia\, Mimi established themself as a talent
 ed singer and guitarist capable of ruminative insight and quietly devastat
 ing song-craft\, inviting comparisons to Laura Marling and Big Thief’s A
 drianne Lenker. The album left deep ripples among many\, picking up accola
 des such as Double J and FBi Radio Feature album and noted by NME as one o
 f their ‘Top 10 album picks’. \n\n\n\nMore about Ruby Gill  \n\n\n\nR
 uby Gill was born and raised in South Africa\, now based in regional VIC\,
  and has spent the last 9 years bringing even the most stoic global audien
 ces to tears with her effortless musicality and powerful poetry. Ruby was 
 recently shortlisted for the Australian Music Prize (top 3 in the country)
  for her ARIA-charting\, globally renowned record ‘Some Kind Of Control\
 ,’ and has toured with the likes of Missy Higgins\, Bongeziwe Mabandla\,
  Nakhane\, Mon Rovia (Liberia)\, Stella Donnelly\, Angie McMahon and more\
 , with Port Fairy Folk Festival’s Emerging Artist of the Year award\, Mu
 sic Victoria’s Best Folk Work nomination\, and The Times’ Breaking Act
  accolade to her name among others. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed
  to an inclusive and safe experience for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair
  accessible with accessible restrooms. We have zero tolerance for harassme
 nt and have support measures in place to ensure everyone’s safety. For s
 pecific accessibility needs or assistance\, please contact us in advance. 
 We aim to make our events enjoyable for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe a
 cknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people\, the Traditional Custodians 
 of the land where our events take place. We pay our respects to their Elde
 rs past\, present\, and emerging\, and recognise their enduring connection
  to this land\, waters\, and culture. We are grateful to celebrate music a
 nd dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T010429Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/ruby-gill-mimi-gilbert-poetry/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Skeleten - Dumbhead - Discoslave
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260321T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260321T230000
DTSTAMP:20260212T132340
UID:ganggang-10001223-1774119600-1774134000@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/01/Poster-tour-2_1-scaled.jpg
CREATED:20260129T221643Z
DESCRIPTION:We’ve been trying to get Skeleten down to GG for a while now
 \, so we’re stoked to be hosting them. Jumping on the bill all the way f
 rom Naarm we also have Dumbhead and local label heads Discoslave \n\n\n\nS
 keleten \n\n\n\nDeeply rooted in Sydney’s tight-knit creative community\
 , Skeleten is a producer\, writer\, singer\, multi-instrumentalist\, DJ\, 
 creative director and visual artist. On his new album Mentalized\, industr
 ial and nu-metal textures underpin dreamlike vocals and abstracted pop arr
 angements\, \n\n\n\nwhile fuzzed-out guitar\, harking back to 2000s indie\
 , punctuates deep house and trip-hop rhythms. Underlying it all is an inna
 te inclination towards the dance music world that Skeleten comes from. \n\
 n\n\nDumbhead \n\n\n\nDumbhead are a three piece from Naarm/Melbourne\, kn
 own for their genre-bending sound. Dumbhead create bass-heavy music built 
 for late-night movement\, drawing from experimental electronica\, triphop\
 , and live beat-making. Their shows are immersive and unpredictable.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260129T221918Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/3193/
END:VEVENT
